  "equipment_type": "Sensor (pressure transmitter)",
  "applies_to": "KELLER X-Line transmitters with RS-485, Class.Group firmware 5.20-10.40 or later, 5.21 and 5.24 (protocol document version 3.7).",
  "summary": "KELLER X-Line digital pressure transmitters (Series 30 and 40) speak both the KELLER bus protocol and Modbus RTU on the same RS-485 line. This map covers the Modbus process values (pressure P1/P2, temperatures and the calculated CH0 channel) as floats, x100 integers and 32-bit integers, the conductivity values of 5.21 devices, and the main configuration and status registers.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "The document gives the start address (StAdd) in hex exactly as it goes into the request; its example reads P1 with start address 0x0002."
  },
  "default_word_order": "ABCD",
  "firmware": "Class.Group 5.20-10.40 and later, 5.21-xx.xx, 5.24-xx.xx (older 5.20-5.50 only supports the floats at 0x0000-0x000A and the 16-bit integers)",
  "source": {
    "title": "Description of the Communication protocol for X-Line Pressure Transmitters from KELLER (Class.Group 5.20, 5.21, 5.24)",
    "doc_number": "Version 3.7",
    "revision_date": "2020-11",
    "url": "https://us.keller-pressure.com/file-cache/website_component/5e2f29419d8b1060a188c377/manuals/1625167998276",
    "pages": "Chapter 4 MODBUS communication, pp. 8-17; float format chapter 6.2, p. 33"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Floats and 32-bit integers are high word first (ABCD): the register map labels the first register HWord, the float chapter puts the exponent byte in register 0, and the worked P1 read returns 3F 75 F0 7B = 0.9607 bar.",
    "Each channel must be read in one request starting on an even address; an odd start returns exception 2.",
    "Inactive channels read NaN (float), 32767 (16-bit) or 2147483647 (32-bit); over/underflow reads +/- infinity in the float range.",
    "Which ranges exist depends on firmware: 32-bit integers need 5.20-12.28 or later; 16-bit integers work on 5.20-5.50 and on 5.20-12.28 or later but not on 5.20-10.40; the 0x0100 block and the 0x02xx configuration range need 5.20-10.40 or later.",
    "Left out: the coefficient ranges (0x03xx, 0x3xxx, 0x40xx), command registers above 0xFF00, conductivity range/compensation settings and the ASCII serial number.",
    "The KELLER bus protocol (functions 30-100) runs on the same line; this map covers only the Modbus functions 3, 6, 8 and 16."
  ],
